#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:3
msgid "Syscall Wrappers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:5
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:7
msgid ""
"All Linux system calls in LLVM-libc are made through wrapper functions in "
"one directory: `src/__support/OSUtil/linux/syscall_wrappers/`. Code outside "
"`src/__support/OSUtil/` does not call `syscall_impl` or use `SYS_*` numbers "
"directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:12
msgid "This provides several benefits:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:14
msgid ""
"**Reusability**: Allows multiple entrypoints to share a single syscall "
"implementation without public APIs depending on other public APIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:16
msgid ""
"**Type Safety**: Using `ErrorOr<T>` ensures that error conditions are "
"handled explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:18
msgid ""
"**Consistency**: Standardizes the conversion of syscall return values into "
"errno-compatible objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:20
msgid ""
"**Maintainability**: Centralizes platform-specific syscall logic, making it "
"easier to audit and update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:23
msgid ""
"The migration of existing code to this structure is still in progress, so "
"the tree contains entrypoints that call `syscall_impl` themselves. Do not "
"copy them. New code uses a wrapper, and adds one if it does not exist yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:27
msgid "The Pattern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:29
msgid ""
"Each syscall has its own header-only library in the `syscall_wrappers` "
"directory. Wrappers live in the `linux_syscalls` namespace to make call "
"sites self-documenting and to clearly identify any leakage into OS-generic "
"code."
msgstr ""

