msgid "Example Wrapper (`src/__support/OSUtil/linux/syscall_wrappers/read.h`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:54
msgid "The entrypoint turns the result into the public contract. In outline:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:67
msgid "Rules for wrappers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:69
msgid ""
"**A wrapper represents an operation of the operating system**, not a POSIX "
"function. Linux-specific system calls get wrappers like any other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:71
msgid ""
"**A wrapper hides which syscall number implements the operation.** Some "
"architectures lack the older syscalls (there is no `SYS_mkdir` on AArch64, "
"for instance), so the `mkdir` wrapper calls `SYS_mkdirat`. Callers do not "
"repeat that choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:75
msgid ""
"**Use `syscall_checked`.** It converts the kernel's error convention into an "
"`ErrorOr<T>`. Do not call `syscall_impl` and check the sign of the result by "
"hand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:78
msgid ""
"**Syscalls that cannot fail return the plain type.** `getpid` returns "
"`pid_t`, not `ErrorOr<pid_t>`, and is one of the few places that use "
"`syscall_impl`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:81
msgid ""
"**A wrapper never sets `errno`.** The entrypoint does. See {ref}"
"`setting_errno`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:84
msgid ""
"Other operating systems follow the same structure under their own directory "
"and namespace, for example `src/__support/OSUtil/freebsd/syscall_wrappers/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:87
msgid "How to Migrate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:89
msgid ""
"**Create the Wrapper**: Add a new header file in `src/__support/OSUtil/linux/"
"syscall_wrappers/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:92
msgid ""
"**Update CMake**: Add a `add_header_library` target for the new wrapper in "
"`src/__support/OSUtil/linux/syscall_wrappers/CMakeLists.txt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:95
msgid "**Refactor Entrypoints**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:97
msgid "Include the new wrapper header (e.g., `read.h`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:98
msgid ""
"Replace direct `syscall_impl` calls with `linux_syscalls::<function_name>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:100
msgid ""
"Update the entrypoint's `DEPENDS` in `CMakeLists.txt` to include the new "
"wrapper target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/syscall_wrapper_refactor.md:103
msgid "Migrate one system call per pull request."
msgstr ""
